 1	\documentclass[11pt]{article}
 2	\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}
 3	\begin{document}
 4	\section*{Problem}
 5	Let $(S_k)_{k \geq 0}$ be the simple random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^2$, and let $T_n$ be the number of steps needed to cover the discrete disc
 6	\[
 7	D_n=\{x \in \mathbb{Z}^2 : \|x\| \leq n\}.
 8	\]
 9	
10	Determine the unique constant $c > 0$ such that the median $m_n$ of $\log T_n$ satisfies
11	\[
12	\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{m_n}{(\log(n))^2} = c.
13	\]
14	
15	\end{document}
